        "subject": "LU-16738 tests: skip conf-sanity/161 if /etc/hosts readonly",
        "message": "LU-16738 tests: skip conf-sanity/161 if /etc/hosts readonly\n\nThe recently-added conf-sanity.sh test_161 was failing in Janitor\ntesting since the /etc/hosts file cannot be modified to add a fake\nMGS hostname to it.\n\nIf a hostname already exists for the MGS then there is no need to\nadd a fake one, making the /etc/hosts read-only status irrelevant.\n\nIf there is no MGS hostname and /etc/hosts is read-only, then skip\nthe end of the test since it needs a hostname and not an IP address.\n\nAdd 'stack_trap cleanup' so a failure doesn't leave a mess behind.\n\nFixes: b850dbb71d (\"LU-16738 utils: add mgsname mount option for custom hostname display\")\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I1e9ae41801192009b08239aeeec7e4d4853ebbe5\nReviewed-on: https://review.whamcloud.com/c/fs/lustre-release/+/66071\nTested-by: jenkins <devops@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nTested-by: Maloo <maloo@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Alex Zhuravlev <bzzz@whamcloud.com>\nReviewed-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
